 in various forms, including ectopic or eutopic secretion, and is often associated with several diseases and conditions that affect the hypothalamic-pituitary axis. It may also occur following pituitary surgery. Management of SIADH is crucial, as it requires careful monitoring and regulation of sodium levels to prevent complications associated with hyponatremia. The syndrome is discussed in medical literature, including the \"\"Manual de Endocrinología y Nutrición,\"\" highlighting its significance in clinical practice.\",62\r\n4023,TOLVAPTÁN,\"Tolvaptán is a medication primarily used to treat hyponatremia, particularly in patients with the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH). It functions by blocking the action of antidiuretic hormone (ADH) in the kidneys, specifically targeting the V2 receptor, which promotes water excretion and induces aquaresis. This mechanism helps to manage sodium levels in patients by facilitating the elimination of excess water from the body.\n\nTolvaptán can be administered in specific dosages, either orally or via nasogastric tube, depending on the patient's nutritional status. It is particularly beneficial for patients experiencing low sodium levels in the blood, including those with heart failure. Overall, tolvaptán serves as a selective vasopressin receptor antagonist that effectively addresses euvolemic hyponatremia by promoting water excretion and helping to restore normal sodium levels.\",11\r\n15072,CONIVAPTÁN,\"Conivaptán is a medication that functions as a vasopressin receptor antagonist, specifically designed to treat hyponatremia, a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood. It is administered intravenously and works by antagonizing the effects of antidiuretic hormone (ADH), thereby helping to restore normal sodium levels in patients.\",2\r\n4029,CARBAMACEPINA,\"Carbamacepina, also known as carbamazepine, is an anticonvulsant medication primarily used to manage seizures in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia. In addition to its anticonvulsant properties, carbamazepine can influence the metabolism of thyroid hormones, which requires monitoring of thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) levels in patients who are hypothyroid. Furthermore, carbamazepine has been associated with the development of the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH), which can impact the duration of treatment. Overall, carbamazepine is a critical medication in seizure management, but it necessitates careful monitoring due to its effects on thyroid function and potential to induce SIADH.\",3\r\n3870,ANTIDEPRESIVOS,\"Los antidepresivos, que incluyen clases como los tricíclicos y los inhibidores de la recaptación de serotonina, son medicamentos utilizados para tratar la depresión y otros trastornos del estado de ánimo. Sin embargo, uno de los efectos secundarios asociados con su uso es la hiperprolactinemia, una condición caracterizada por niveles elevados de prolactina en la sangre.\",2\r\n4039,ANALOGOS DE VASOPRESINA,\"Los análogos de vasopresina son medicamentos que imitan la acción de la vasopresina, y algunos pueden estar implicados en el desarrollo del SIADH.\",1\r\n4038,ANTIDIABETICOS,\"Los antidiabéticos son medicamentos utilizados para controlar la diabetes, y algunos de ellos están relacionados con el SIADH.\",1\r\n15033,BLOQUE: SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO,\"A section or block focused on advanced nutritional support, particularly in relation to maintaining body water in threatening situations\",1\r\n4028,CLORPROPAMIDA,Clorpropamida is a medication that can cause SIADH,1\r\n15245,CONIVAPTAN,\"Conivaptan is a medication used for the treatment of hyponatremia, particularly in patients with euvolemic hyponatremia.\",1\r\n4030,CÁNCER PULMONAR DE CÉLULAS PEQUEÑAS,Small cell lung cancer is a type of cancer that can cause ectopic production of vasopressin leading to SIADH,1\r\n15049,ELLISON DH,\"Ellison DH is a researcher who contributed to the understandin